/* the Sheriff's Station */
$ST_BODY = "The Santa Clarita Valley Sheriff's Station is the Los Angeles County Sheriff's Department station that polices the valley: the City of Santa Clarita and the unincorporated communities around it, from Castaic and Val Verde to Stevenson Ranch and Sand Canyon.[1] The City has no police department of its own. It contracts with the County for police services, and the station's captain serves as its chief of police; the captain since August 2025 is Brandon Barclay.[2][3]\n\nThe station began as Substation No. 6, opened on 26 August 1926 in a former house at the northeast corner of Spruce Street and Sixth Street in Newhall, today's Main and Sixth.[4][5] In 1972 it moved to the County Civic Center, at 23740 Magic Mountain Parkway in Valencia.[5][6] The present station, at 26201 Golden Valley Road, was built by the City and the County together: ground was broken on 25 July 2018, the ribbon was cut on 18 October 2021, and the station went into service in November 2021.[6][7][8]";
$ST_NOTES = ['Los Angeles County Sheriff\'s Department, "Santa Clarita Valley Station," https://lasd.org/santa-clarita-valley/, read 4 October 2026: 26201 Golden Valley Road; the areas it serves, among them the City of Santa Clarita, Castaic, Val Verde, Stevenson Ranch and Sand Canyon.',
