/* the church */
$CH_BODY = "Santa Clarita Baptist Church, at 27249 Luther Drive in Canyon Country, was formed in 1981 when two Baptist congregations a mile apart merged: the First Baptist Church of Saugus and Temple Baptist Church of Canyon Country.[1][2] By the church's own history, the merged congregation first met under its new name on 31 May 1981, on the First Baptist site, where building had begun in 1968. First Baptist had begun on 19 November 1962, meeting in Amos Clemmons's garage; Temple Baptist first met on 11 January 1976.[1] In 1982 the church founded Santa Clarita Christian School, on the same campus.[3]";
$CH_NOTES = ['Santa Clarita Baptist Church, "Our History," as captured by the Wayback Machine on October 6, 2016, https://web.archive.org/web/20161006144241/http://www.scbc.cc:80/our-history/. The church\'s own account: the dates rest on it alone.',
