/* Newhall Elementary */
$NE_BODY = "Newhall Elementary School is the Newhall School District's first and oldest school. The district was formed on 10 May 1877, on the petition of J.F. Powell and 47 others, and where its first classes met is not known.[1][2] It is not the valley's oldest school: the Sulphur Springs district dates from September 1872.[3]\n\nIn 1878, after the new town of Newhall had moved two miles south to its present site, classes were held in a building on the Sanford Lyon ranch, a corner of Addi Lyon's bunkhouse, which Leon Worden places roughly where the Valencia Marketplace stands today.[4][2][5] The first schoolhouse, believed to date from 1879 and paid for largely by Judge Powell, at $3,500, stood at the northeast corner of Ninth and Walnut streets: two storeys, with a hall upstairs where Sunday school met.[4][2][6] It burned in May 1890; the Los Angeles Herald of 4 June reported that the school had \"burned down at that place a few days ago.\"[7] It was rebuilt on the same site that year, again of two storeys, with help from H.C. Needham.[4][2][8]\n\nThe third school stood near the northwest corner of Newhall Avenue and what is now Lyons Avenue. The sources disagree on when and why: the Newhall History Project of 1940 dates it to 1911 and says the old site had grown too small, while Jerry Reynolds dates it to 1914, after a fire that no contemporary report has been found to confirm.[4][9][2] Pupils went on to San Fernando High School after it opened in 1896, and in 1932 the district acquired a 31-seat bus.[2][10]\n\nThe fourth school, on Walnut Street at Eleventh, opened on 14 September 1925. That August the Newhall Signal had invited parents to inspect \"the new school house\", and in November the old Lyons Avenue property was sold to A.B. Perkins. Wings were added in 1930.[11][12][13] Some later accounts, among them Reynolds's, give 1928.[9] Fire destroyed all but the north wing early on 14 February 1939, and the present building was first occupied on 10 May 1940, on the same site, now 24607 North Walnut Street.[14][4][15]";
